@tradition playlist-duel
// Round 2: two people play three songs each from Imani O'Neill's playlists and the room picks a winner. Every 4 weeks from week 9 (Days 57, 85...).
// Rules: FX24 (0.93.2, behind TRAD_0932_ON in section 13). Words: CS1 (plans/trad-0932-words.txt, claude/crew-stories-pitch 7b1e7300).
// Host check (FX24): Imani's late garden shift ends at 21:00 (free from 21:15), so 21:15-22:00, not the card's 21:00.
k: 1310
title: Playlist duel
when: every 4 weeks monday week 1 from day 57
at: 21:15-22:00
min: 20
to-bed: yes
where: 4 pool music
hold: 1
who: oneill-imani always, music 45%, musician 30%, night-owl 20%, everyone 8%
anim: talk
host: oneill-imani
from: oneill-imani
invite: host=oneill-imani odds=25% line="Playlist duel. Three songs each, the room votes. I always lose. On purpose."

== mail
- Playlist duel tomorrow, {time}, the music room. Two playlists, three songs each, the room picks. I host. I always lose. On purpose.

== ask
- Playlist duel in the music room. Imani's lost four in a row. On purpose, she says.   #funny
- Bring a song for the playlist duel. Not the lighthouse one. Everybody brings that.   #funny
- Coming to the playlist duel? Vote for the one with the drums.

== here
- Song two. Oh, that's a good one.
- Hands up for the left side. Now the right.
- That's not fair. That's my favourite.   #funny
- Next! No skipping.

== thanks
- Two people play three songs each, and the room votes for its favourite. Imani loses again, and insists she let them win.   #funny

== chatter
- Imani lost the playlist duel again. She says it was a strategy.   #funny
- Somebody played a song from home at the playlist duel and won by a mile.
- I've had one song in my head since the playlist duel. Send help.   #funny
